<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reggio Calabria</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rhegium</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reggio <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a> is the largest city of Calabria in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the Strait of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/messina">Messina</a> facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. It was founded as the Greek colony of Rhegion in the 8th century BCE and later became the Roman Rhegium. Rebuilt after the earthquake of 1908, it houses the Riace bronzes in its national archaeological museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reggio-calabria.jpg" alt="Reggio Calabria" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mimmo Zema · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reggio_calabria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
